-- Passage rg4-comparing-texts-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('78660014-1c67-52fc-83eb-1cfededf61e9', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Small but Smart$q$, $q$Text 1: The Mouse and the Elephant (a story from India)

In a village near the river, an elephant liked to stand in the only shady spot by the well. No one else could rest there. The animals were too afraid to ask him to move.

A little mouse named Chotu had an idea. He climbed onto a branch above the elephant and said, "Friend, the shade is cooler down by the river. The water there tickles your toes."

The elephant wanted cool toes, so he walked to the river. He loved it so much that he stayed. Now the other animals could rest by the well. Chotu sat with them and smiled.

Text 2: The Tall Shelf (a story from Peru)

Luz was the smallest girl in her class. One day the teacher put the art box on a high shelf, and then left the room. The tall kids jumped and stretched, but no one could reach it.

Luz looked around. She took a long broom from the corner. Gently, she hooked the handle under the box and slid it to the edge. Her friend Mateo caught it.

When the teacher came back, everyone was painting. "Who reached the box?" she asked. The class pointed at Luz.$q$, 'draft')
