insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('91936365-a52f-5ba6-8fc3-638bcfa85e3b', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Finding Home$q$, $q$Text 1: The Smell of Home (a story from Pakistan and England)

Bilal's family moved from Lahore to a rainy town in England. Everything felt strange. The streets were quiet, and the air smelled of wet leaves instead of spices.

At school, Bilal ate lunch alone. Then one day, his mother packed warm parathas. A boy named Owen sniffed the air. "What is that? It smells amazing," he said. Bilal shared half. Owen shared his apple.

That weekend, Owen came over to learn how to roll parathas. Flour got everywhere. Bilal laughed for the first time in weeks. The rainy town felt a little more like home.

Text 2: First Snow (a poem from Peru and Canada)

In Lima, the ocean was warm.
Here, the wind bites my nose.
I miss my abuela's kitchen
and the songs on the radio.

Then my neighbor, Mei,
knocks on my door one day.
"It's snowing! Come outside!"
She shows me how to play.

We build a snow friend, tall and round.
I give it my red scarf from home.
Now a little piece of Lima
stands in Canada's snow.$q$, 'draft')
